    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `initials` field needed to appear in the `GET /api/owners/{id}` JSON response, which serializes an `OwnerDto` (generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by MapStruct's `OwnerMapper`). Following the existing `displayName` computed-field pattern, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` has the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression computing initials as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\" +\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n\nFor `\"john\"`/`\"smith\"` this yields `\"J.S.\"`, matching the acceptance test. `./mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with all tests passing.",
